{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters","id":1476534,"title":"Why the struggle matters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-16T14:57:50-07:00","id":1476534,"title":"Why the struggle matters","content":"I've been in this fandom for years, long enough that certain mentalities have become familiar to me. In light of the 5th edition news, I thought I'd address why I think this mentality is missing the point of WtA.<br /> <br /> The typical idea goes like this; &quot;Gaia is dead, there is no hope at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why this idea bothers me so much and why I feel it does not fit WtA, is that so much of WtA is about the struggle. Garou fight and argue and die to gain an inch of a better future. They might not succeed, but they must still try.<br /> <br /> It is this trying that makes the game for me. The desperate struggle against overwhelming odds is 90% of the game. At least for me. Not only does it reflect how it feels to be faced with IRL wrongs, but also it gives the garou pcs something to do. A clear motivation.<br /> <br /> Aside from the fact that if Gaia goes the universe does as well. If Gaia is dead and the fight is over, what exactly is the throughline of the game? If there is no longer a struggle, so much of the core WtA play no longer applies. The garou are no longer fighting against the odds, they lost and are now living on borrowed time until the universe keels over.<br /> <br /> This is actually a similar situation to if the garou had won. Loss of the overarching goal means suddenly there is nothing really for the garou to do.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing the idea is that despite Gaia dying, the garou would continue the war against the Wyrm. But that lessens the impact of Gaia dying in my mind.<br /> <br /> This is rambly, but I wanted to give my thoughts on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T15:26:00-07:00","id":1476536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters#post1476534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been in this fandom for years, long enough that certain mentalities have become familiar to me. In light of the 5th edition news, I thought I'd address why I think this mentality is missing the point of WtA.<br /> <br /> The typical idea goes like this; &amp;quot;Gaia is dead, there is no hope at all.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Why this idea bothers me so much and why I feel it does not fit WtA, is that so much of WtA is about the struggle. Garou fight and argue and die to gain an inch of a better future. They might not succeed, but they must still try.<br /> <br /> It is this trying that makes the game for me. The desperate struggle against overwhelming odds is 90% of the game. At least for me. Not only does it reflect how it feels to be faced with IRL wrongs, but also it gives the garou pcs something to do. A clear motivation.<br /> <br /> Aside from the fact that if Gaia goes the universe does as well. If Gaia is dead and the fight is over, what exactly is the throughline of the game? If there is no longer a struggle, so much of the core WtA play no longer applies. The garou are no longer fighting against the odds, they lost and are now living on borrowed time until the universe keels over.<br /> <br /> This is actually a similar situation to if the garou had won. Loss of the overarching goal means suddenly there is nothing really for the garou to do.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing the idea is that despite Gaia dying, the garou would continue the war against the Wyrm. But that lessens the impact of Gaia dying in my mind.<br /> <br /> This is rambly, but I wanted to give my thoughts on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should point out that even in the very beggining if 5e wod. The idea was never Gaia is dead. It has been Gaia is dying. It was a time where the garou nation was in it's possible moment,but it was never a hopeless game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T20:35:12-07:00","id":1476547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476536#post1476536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should point out that even in the very beggining if 5e wod. The idea was never Gaia is dead. It has been Gaia is dying. It was a time where the garou nation was in it's possible moment,but it was never a hopeless game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given info in this post: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information#post1463892\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...on#post1463892</a><br /> <br /> I'd say we are going for a Gaia is dead narrative.<br /> <br /> But in any case, my issue is mostly why that plotline is suggested. Often it seems to imply that the setting is not dark enough. That the garou fighting the odds is too heroic and bright. Which in my opinion is missing the point of the game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T23:34:17-07:00","id":1476555,"title":"","content":"It might be an overreaction to the heroic high fantasy aspects of Revised. I thought many aspects of that era was more like a typical D&amp;D campaign against a dark lord than the morally complex setting originally portrayed in 1e/early 2e.<br /> <br /> But if so, it's another piece of evidence of why I hate metaplot. The exact nature and current situation of the Garou's struggle is something best set by individual STs for their own chronicles. There's no problem if an individual ST wants to run a chronicle where the struggle seems over and the last survivors are killing time until the end. A &quot;Wolf's Rain&quot; style chronicle could be very fun. But it's not the only kind of story to tell. And chronicles where the Apocalypse might be decades or centuries away is just as vital to the game as ones where it seems imminent. All sorts of stories are fun. I always like the implied threat that PCs might be living in the end times, or the precursor to the end times, but it's not needed to make that explicitly so.<br /> <br /> Making a canonical decision invalidates what many STs are doing and unnecessarily divides fandom. Instead of telling us what to do, the game should be providing us tools to tell the stories we want, and illustrating options available to STs through local sourcebooks that can emphasize aspects of the game without telling us the entire world setting is like that.<br /> <br /> I personally find it silly when games tell us, &quot;Yeah, Gehenna or the Apocalypse or whatever has already happened.&quot; The world can only end once. This idea that a major event like the Apocalypse has happened, but nobody seems to notice rings false to me. I always viewed that Gehenna/Apocalypse/Ascension/Doomsday/Endless Winter is an end of the world event that blatantly reveals the supernatural is real and forever changes Earth. How the Hellboy/BPRD comics approached this is more along the lines of how I envision the scenario playing out. The official WoD products have just been sad and pathetic in comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T01:26:45-07:00","id":1476559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476555#post1476555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally find it silly when games tell us, &quot;Yeah, Gehenna or the Apocalypse or whatever has already happened.&quot; The world can only end once. This idea that a major event like the Apocalypse has happened, but nobody seems to notice rings false to me. I always viewed that Gehenna/Apocalypse/Ascension/Doomsday/Endless Winter is an end of the world event that blatantly reveals the supernatural is real and forever changes Earth. How the Hellboy/BPRD comics approached this is more along the lines of how I envision the scenario playing out. The official WoD products have just been sad and pathetic in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It is one thing to make a side game for Post-Apocalypse. But to say that the world ended only for the supernatural, especially in a game where the forces at play affect everything. It feels like they wanted to get rid of the ticking clock entirely, or wanted more free hands to do things \u00e0 la CotD.<br /> <br /> Regardless, it entirely misses the point of the game and lessens the importance of what garou fight for.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T07:33:11-07:00","id":1476578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476536#post1476536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point out that even in the very beggining if 5e wod. The idea was never Gaia is dead. It has been Gaia is dying. It was a time where the garou nation was in it's possible moment,but it was never a hopeless game.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the purpose of the problem in discussion, the difference is just semantics, although I agree we should see the final product before passing a more definite judgement.<br /> <br /> But assuming what seems to be the plot to be told, dead or dying doesn't change that the final fight already happened and was lost, and now the Garou live in a post-Apocalypse where they scrap for a living for whatever time they still have instead of there being a glimpse of any true hope to undo Gaia's state and fate. It is survival in a dying world, not raging for a better one, and the characters that still cling to hope are, for canonical and narrative purposes, simply deluded.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> said, this isn't a bad premise on its own in any way. But it is limiting for the setting we're discussing and misses the point of the game entirely. It is a good new game, but a terrible core W:tA edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T08:14:58-07:00","id":1476580,"title":"","content":"I think a world where there is no hope doesn't make sense. If Gaia was dead, in a final sense, not dying/comatose/sleeping/sick, then this camp that sought to flee Gaia via the umbra to other planets/dimensions/whatever where right all along and nothing Garou did do mattered (being a dump on those who played 1st to revised Edition and well into the X20-era) and it doesn't make sense to start a new game in a 5th Edition - for it is hopeless.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are games where that doesn't matter. I once played a game on the premise that every character would die. There were teelights in the middle of the game table in a dark room, and at least when the last one would go out, every character was dead. Still it was a fun game about moral with all the characters on a ship in a Titanic-like scenario.<br /> But would it be material for chronicles and ongoing gaming - no, it wouldn't.<br /> <br /> I think that line along the lines of &quot;Gehenna/Apocalypse is over&quot; turned up in the X20-era (especially that one Technocracy convent book revised never published), because authors and developers weren't sure on what the direction for the game lines was, back then when CCP had control of the property and the decision was made to allow OPP to produce more books than just X20 single volumes. And from all I see in V5th it is not post-gehenna. It is a meta-plot time-jump with a lot of changes to the Setting that are more or less accepted by the fans of the games up until the X20-era.<br /> <br /> We got a similar meta-plot time-jump situation when BNS presented it's WtA-Setting. And I have now idea how well accepted these changes are in the LARP scene that uses MET. All chronicles I know in Germany don't use MET or the Setting by BNS.<br /> <br /> At Paradox there is the possibility that the decision makers go two different ways. Make radical changes to rules and Setting, or make only those changes that are required by the V5th meta-plot (but tone them down), only make changes to the game mechanics and rules, but leave the Setting more or less untouched...<br /> They could go a way, where the company developing W5 is allowed to make drastic changes but OPP might still be books based on X20-era materials and rules. But I doubt that. I haven't seen the release plan for OPP, but iirc they also started to make V5 supplementals and I don't see any vampire stuff for V20 anymore...<br /> <br /> I fear, that W5 will be not to my liking and that W20 material will cease to appear.<br /> Maybe I should pre-emptively switch to Steve Jackson's WtA for GURPS......<br /> <br /> <br /> But, yeah, the struggle is necessary for WtA. And it is about topics that matter, not just survival.<br /> It's Werewolf: the Apocalypse.<br /> Not Werewolf: Apocalypse Now<br /> Not Werewolf: Post-Apocalypse<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T14:00:57-07:00","id":1476878,"title":"","content":"So, Gaia is dying. She\u2019s been dying. But there is still the struggle. Achilli had posted on Twitter that he wants every victory to feel big. The umbra is hostile, wyrm runs rampant and you\u2019re fighting to reclaim every inch of territory you can. <br /> <br /> The nation is splintered, the new cubs don\u2019t even know if the mythology is simply mythology or is what any elders say is actually real. Turns to the focus back to that first Ed personal horror and ambiguous meta plot vibe. <br /> <br /> First edition made it a point to not say with the apocalypse is real or a garou legend. I suspect that\u2019s the same vibe they\u2019re going for. It also mentioned previous wars against the wyrm where the garou won and beat the forces back for centuries. They\u2019ve been here before I think, the garou that is. <br /> <br /> We\u2019re gonna have to see how the game shapes up on launch. I suspect the worlds structure will change in such to accommodate vampire since one world of darkness and all that. Sounds like a bad thing at first but\u2026 I dunno I\u2019m not so sure. Vampire is the poster child for WoD, the money maker. Might not be so bad to have a coherent world that features more cyclical end times rather than a gigantic \u201cworld is ending guys.\u201d This would key in with events like the storm eater in Wild West. <br /> <br /> Tldr, I believe we\u2019ll find plenty of struggle when 5th drops, but also\u2026 I\u2019m thinking a lot more player agency with regards to the meta and werewolf society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T15:19:59-07:00","id":1476891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476878#post1476878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Gaia is dying. She\u2019s been dying. But there is still the struggle. Achilli had posted on Twitter that he wants every victory to feel big. The umbra is hostile, wyrm runs rampant and you\u2019re fighting to reclaim every inch of territory you can.<br /> <br /> The nation is splintered, the new cubs don\u2019t even know if the mythology is simply mythology or is what any elders say is actually real. Turns to the focus back to that first Ed personal horror and ambiguous meta plot vibe.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, we already have game that does all these things and does them really well. Werewolf the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <br /> In a world like that, there is no longer the Apocalypse struggle. It is the gang territory struggle. The Apocalypse struggle is knowing the days are counting down, things are far from perfect, but you must try or everything is lost. Point is, the garou -haven't- lost yet in WtA. They still have the wild areas and the umbra, their caerns and such. But if they lose, then all that is lost.<br /> <br /> The 5th edition basically starts a game which theme is the end of the world and erases all the dread of that by just taking everything dear for the garou away on the outset. It is an entirely different beast and situation from the previous ones.<br /> <br /> Besides as Black Fox said, the world can only end once. And this game is called Apocalypse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T16:13:02-07:00","id":1476896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476891#post1476891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, we already have game that does all these things and does them really well. Werewolf the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <br /> In a world like that, there is no longer the Apocalypse struggle. It is the gang territory struggle. The Apocalypse struggle is knowing the days are counting down, things are far from perfect, but you must try or everything is lost. Point is, the garou -haven't- lost yet in WtA. They still have the wild areas and the umbra, their caerns and such. But if they lose, then all that is lost.<br /> <br /> The 5th edition basically starts a game which theme is the end of the world and erases all the dread of that by just taking everything dear for the garou away on the outset. It is an entirely different beast and situation from the previous ones.<br /> <br /> Besides as Black Fox said, the world can only end once. And this game is called Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that 20th (and first) tried to stay away from the idea of the apocalypse as an absolute. With 20th injecting hope with the 8th sign. I mean I don\u2019t see achilli tossing the entire meta out. We simply don\u2019t know yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T18:15:08-07:00","id":1476906,"title":"","content":"Well said, Ana Mizuki. The struggle to save the world, and the tiny splinter of hope that they can, is the entire reason and the only reason I want to play Werewolf. Get rid of the Umbra and caerns, make Gaia dead or unsalvageable, and the game instantly becomes 100% pointless.<br /> <br /> I have no desire whatsoever to play Forsaken, ever. I'm sure it's a great game, but it has less than Zero appeal for me. I also have no interest in playing Kult, or a game based on I Have No Mouth And I Must Scream. I want to play the fight to save Gaia, the fight to make the world better even just a little bit, the fight to save that bit of forest, that Umbral glade, that reef, that caern. It's the same reason I have Zero interest in Mage Revised. If the fight is over and we lost, then the game is over, goodbye.<br /> <br /> I welcomed the bit of hope injected into the game by Revised and the Eighth Prophecy. The real world is dark enough. Werewolf was already plenty dark and horrific. It did not need to be so hopeless that there's no point in picking up the dice.<br /> <br /> If OPP was allowed to continue publishing W20 for the fans and players of the original game, and this one came out as a third version of Werewolf, I'd be fine. But they've made it clear that W20 is cancelled and they will never allow another real Werewolf book to see print. They even cancelled the Bunyip Tribebook that was being written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-21-2022, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T21:41:56-07:00","id":1476919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476896#post1476896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worth noting that 20th (and first) tried to stay away from the idea of the apocalypse as an absolute. With 20th injecting hope with the 8th sign. I mean I don\u2019t see achilli tossing the entire meta out. We simply don\u2019t know yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a vast difference between the 8th sign being of hope and MAYBE they could win the Apocalypse- And the way 5th edition is sounding. At the very least, it is using the very same methods WtF used when it was released to distance itself from WtA.<br /> <br /> I do not intend that Achili is being malicious, not at all. It's just very odd to me that the way the 5th edition is changing is very similar to the way WtF works, when the two games have entirely different moods.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T22:02:27-07:00","id":1476920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476919#post1476919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a vast difference between the 8th sign being of hope and MAYBE they could win the Apocalypse- And the way 5th edition is sounding. At the very least, it is using the very same methods WtF used when it was released to distance itself from WtA.<br /> <br /> I do not intend that Achili is being malicious, not at all. It's just very odd to me that the way the 5th edition is changing is very similar to the way WtF works, when the two games have entirely different moods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand why you think that. And while forsaken 2nd does, the skeleton of forsaken first edition, which is an achilli product, does bare a lot of the original themes of apocalypse first edition. Being that the purpose of the uratha is acceptance of a responsibility, theirs before time, to maintain a balance in the world. A lot of the core elements are similar. At least there. Or maybe I\u2019ve been philosophizing the game lines entirely too much over the last two months, which is entirely possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T00:27:03-07:00","id":1476927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476920#post1476920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can understand why you think that. And while forsaken 2nd does, the skeleton of forsaken first edition, which is an achilli product, does bare a lot of the original themes of apocalypse first edition. Being that the purpose of the uratha is acceptance of a responsibility, theirs before time, to maintain a balance in the world. A lot of the core elements are similar. At least there. Or maybe I\u2019ve been philosophizing the game lines entirely too much over the last two months, which is entirely possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, 1st ed. Forsaken kind of suffered from not having an identity of its own. Mind, it did eventually develop it and I'm a big fan of the game.<br /> <br /> Just that, maybe Apocalypse should not follow those elements, since Forsaken exists already.<br /> <br /> One thing that utterly baffles me and has baffled me for years, is the push for a hostile umbra in so many sources. Avatar Storm for Mage in Revised, BNS and Changing Ways and now 5th ed. trying for that in WtA. Is the umbra really that much of a cheat that it needs to be limited?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T02:24:29-07:00","id":1476935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476927#post1476927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, 1st ed. Forsaken kind of suffered from not having an identity of its own. Mind, it did eventually develop it and I'm a big fan of the game.<br /> <br /> Just that, maybe Apocalypse should not follow those elements, since Forsaken exists already.<br /> <br /> One thing that utterly baffles me and has baffled me for years, is the push for a hostile umbra in so many sources. Avatar Storm for Mage in Revised, BNS and Changing Ways and now 5th ed. trying for that in WtA. Is the umbra really that much of a cheat that it needs to be limited?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think it\u2019s limiting it. We don\u2019t know that they\u2019re cutting elements of the umbra. Just that it\u2019s going to be more dangerous. I had a peek at apocalyptic records manuscript and there\u2019s a mention of some interesting bane activity. Less forsaken and more\u2026 the wyrm is just winning the prolonged conflict. <br /> <br /> A similar argument I see is that it\u2019s going to lessen the importance of Theurges, and I don\u2019t agree at all. Infact I see theurges being MORE important for the future of the line. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also been on this positivity kick lately, so instead of approaching things as \u201coh god why\u201d I\u2019m going for \u201cwell if this is different what awesome freaky thing am I going to see?!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T03:12:31-07:00","id":1476941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476927#post1476927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that utterly baffles me and has baffled me for years, is the push for a hostile umbra in so many sources. Avatar Storm for Mage in Revised, BNS and Changing Ways and now 5th ed. trying for that in WtA. Is the umbra really that much of a cheat that it needs to be limited?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was this sense in the older editions that the game had pulled too far away from its &quot;gritty street level&quot; roots and become too high fantasy. This was especially true for Mage (where you had things like the Technocracy operating in full Star Trek mode with dyson spheres and fleets of starships) but even in Werewolf the game had begun to focus so much on the big, grand ideas that the smaller ideas were getting lost. So there was this real push to par down the Umbra and refocus the gamelines back onto the real world. So the Umbra began to written as more hostile and dangerous, and crossing over was much more difficult, so that players would end up spending less time there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T04:12:37-07:00","id":1476944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476941#post1476941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was this sense in the older editions that the game had pulled too far away from its &quot;gritty street level&quot; roots and become too high fantasy. This was especially true for Mage (where you had things like the Technocracy operating in full Star Trek mode with dyson spheres and fleets of starships) but even in Werewolf the game had begun to focus so much on the big, grand ideas that the smaller ideas were getting lost. So there was this real push to par down the Umbra and refocus the gamelines back onto the real world. So the Umbra began to written as more hostile and dangerous, and crossing over was much more difficult, so that players would end up spending less time there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree.<br /> <br /> Basically, the game should be about the PCs' sept and their home turf. Especially revised, I found, focused to strongly on global interactions and how the tribes were organised globally - and plots that were globally relevant. I mean, tribe novels, sure a nice read, but it is an epic about an eternal being, not your typical Street Level story, like 1st Editons Wyrm Wolf was. Or most of the &quot;When will you Rage?&quot;-stories.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind a shift in tone to refocus the game onto local issues. Away from the global problems and the globalisation in general. I mean, sure, globalisation has its own dangers and there surely are things we, as mankind, should start to get a better handle on and so should the fictional garou, but as foundation for the game, more localised, character-driven focus might be nice to have.<br /> <br /> But, there are also players who think differently. And that is alright. There is not a single right way to play the game.<br /> <br /> What I fear is, that changes in the Setting force the rules to change force the way the game is played to change in a way, that one can't get back to the way the game was played before.<br /> For example, if there is a more hostile Umbra, it will affect umbra travel rules, gifts, side stepping, and so on. And these newer rules will so depend on the changes to setting, that they won't work with a game world that has the Umbra still as it is in revised/W20....<br /> This, for me, would drastically minimize the value of the newer material.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T05:06:14-07:00","id":1476948,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'm not sure what a &quot;more hostile&quot; Umbra really means. The Umbra is pretty hostile. Sure, some of the Realms are really cool for certain characters, but others are utter hell. Even a normal urban/suburban Penumbra is Weaver heavy enough that one wrong step could get you tangling in pattern webs.<br /> <br /> To me, the thing that might need to change (and has less direct mechanical impacts) is the relationship of spirits and Garou. While this is closer to Forsaken in a lot of ways, it's not necessarily that the spirits need to be more hostile, but they need to be more selfish and alien. Gaian spirits are part of a generations long pact that basically turns them from interesting NPCs in their own right, to hoops to jump through to get various stuff. There's not any real point to getting into the personality and quirks that separate any two given spirits of the same brood besides players/the ST finding doing so fun. The more spirits are emphasized as dangerous not because they hate the Garou, but because they're just extremely difficult to understand and their interests are never fully aligned with the Garou, the more interesting and varied spirit focused parts of play get to be. Too much spirit interactions in WtA boil down to, &quot;you can easily fast forward past a bunch of formalities and get on with whatever mechanical widget you're after,&quot; or, &quot;hunt and maybe kill it.&quot; It's too &quot;safe&quot; in a sense of predictability and boring certainty of what will happen, rather than there always being an edge of risk even in the best of circumstances.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T08:40:47-07:00","id":1476964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476948#post1476948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'm not sure what a &quot;more hostile&quot; Umbra really means. The Umbra is pretty hostile. Sure, some of the Realms are really cool for certain characters, but others are utter hell. Even a normal urban/suburban Penumbra is Weaver heavy enough that one wrong step could get you tangling in pattern webs.<br /> <br /> To me, the thing that might need to change (and has less direct mechanical impacts) is the relationship of spirits and Garou. While this is closer to Forsaken in a lot of ways, it's not necessarily that the spirits need to be more hostile, but they need to be more selfish and alien. Gaian spirits are part of a generations long pact that basically turns them from interesting NPCs in their own right, to hoops to jump through to get various stuff. There's not any real point to getting into the personality and quirks that separate any two given spirits of the same brood besides players/the ST finding doing so fun. The more spirits are emphasized as dangerous not because they hate the Garou, but because they're just extremely difficult to understand and their interests are never fully aligned with the Garou, the more interesting and varied spirit focused parts of play get to be. Too much spirit interactions in WtA boil down to, &quot;you can easily fast forward past a bunch of formalities and get on with whatever mechanical widget you're after,&quot; or, &quot;hunt and maybe kill it.&quot; It's too &quot;safe&quot; in a sense of predictability and boring certainty of what will happen, rather than there always being an edge of risk even in the best of circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would fit with with this tweet from Achilli:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://&amp;quot;I think maybe there&#39;s a misunderstanding here. There are no plans to downplay the Umbra, but rather to re-examine the Garou&#39;s relationship with it.&amp;quot;-From Achilli&#39;s twitterhttps://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1504437752628133896?s=20&amp;t=OgapZK_xtDRYk6ktEM5uNQ\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;I think maybe there's a misunderstanding here. There are no plans to downplay the Umbra, but rather to re-examine the Garou's relationship with it.&quot;</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T08:51:26-07:00","id":1476965,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> on that one. If there is one thing I think Apocalypse needs correction is that spirits are described in such a way that their allegiance in the global scheme matters so much more than the spirit itself, the last one generally being just a bunch of formalities you need to go through and the list of benefits for interacting with it.<br /> <br /> Other than that, though, while I personally prefer Forsaken ten times over Apocalypse, it is mostly a matter of taste. Making them the same game is pointless, as Forsaken itself already proved in 1st ed, making Apocalypse become another Forsaken is even worse!<br /> <br /> \u200bNow, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1939_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1939\" data-vbnamecard=\"1939\">Lyrics Of War</a> has one point here: we're mostly conjecturing for now. It doesn't matter how likely it is to be what we fear it will be, we're not discussing yet a realized game. We can't say for sure how things will really be in the end, not only regarding to our conjectures, but also to whatever elements they add that we don't expect.<br /> <br /> But the core problem is the identity of the game. An awesome game that isn't anything like W:tA shouldn't be called W:tA and shouldn't take its place in the setting. Period. Not throwing the metaplot aside has zero to do with this, metaplot is <i>setting</i>, not game. The game is setting + genre, themes and mood. If the setting evolves to support <b><i>other</i></b> themes, genre and mood <b><i>in substitution</i></b> to the old ones, something's very wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476878#post1476878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect the worlds structure will change in such to accommodate vampire since one world of darkness and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a point I'm really curious about how they'll try to pull it out.<br /> <br /> A One WoD is a problem. The lines are evidently connected, but ultimately are each their own version of the setting instead of the same setting, because they invalidate a lot of assumptions of each other.<br /> <br /> I don't see a One World happening without some sacrifices, and I don't think Werewolf will get the better end of it, but I'm really curious to see what sort of stunt they pull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T09:39:13-07:00","id":1476974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476964#post1476964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that would fit with with this tweet from Achilli:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://&amp;quot;I think maybe there&#39;s a misunderstanding here. There are no plans to downplay the Umbra, but rather to re-examine the Garou&#39;s relationship with it.&amp;quot;-From Achilli&#39;s twitter https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1504437752628133896?s=20&amp;t=OgapZK_xtDRYk6ktEM5uNQ\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;I think maybe there's a misunderstanding here. There are no plans to downplay the Umbra, but rather to re-examine the Garou's relationship with it.&quot;</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that sounds a lot better. Mind, I'll still be skeptical until I see the book. But as long as its not an Avatar Storm or Hisil deal, it might work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T12:21:51-07:00","id":1476998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1476941#post1476941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there was this real push to par down the Umbra and refocus the gamelines back onto the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your post.<br /> <br /> I think a problem with many games is that while we got a lot of description of the greater Umbra with its various Near Realms and other big concepts like the Dream Zone, that the books told us very little about how to design the local Penumbra. So ironically there was better support for STs to run a grand umbral adventure than one in the Penumbra strongly tied to the real world.<br /> <br /> Personally, I found it to be a very big gap in terms of what was described about the Penumbra, and how I should be presenting it as an ST. There are all sorts of details to figure out. How many Domains should there be locally and where? How do I describe Domains and their connection to the Penumbra? How many Moon Paths should I place and their destinations? What should the spirit population be like? How do I balance the needs of non-Theurges to interact with spirits versus how to keep Theurges vital and feel needed? What are the typical hazards in the Penumbra I should present to players so that talens like Moon Glows are useful?<br /> <br /> For example, if we had been provided a local Penumbra map for NYC in Rage Across New York, it would have been very instructive for STs. Or at least one example of such in the other Rage books, or in one of the ST Handbooks or Umbra books so we could see a variety of different Penumbras (urban, suburban, rural, wilderness, etc.) and show STs how to build them one's self, then we'd likely have STs concentrate more on local Penumbra and tie it into their local septs and protectorates.<br /> <br /> With examples, STs could still be empowered to make things LESS or MORE active, populated, dangerous, etc. than what was given. But without examples, I think most STs had too much to figure out and left the Penumbra a blank, uninteresting spot.<br /> <br /> In practice, I generally saw STs handwave the local Penumbra away UNLESS they had a specific plot to do there. Instead, the Umbra was used mostly when there was something to be done concerning one of the Near Realms because they had much more direction and inspiration there.<br /> <br /> I wasn't satisfied with my own STing of the Umbra so I made it a project to figure out the bolts and nuts of portraying the local Penumbra, cobbling together various details mentioned in the corebook, Umbra books, Players and STs guides, and elsewhere, and then deciding how to implement those details in practice. I've finally gotten something I am comfortable running. But it took a lot of work to figure out those details.<br /> <br /> IF that is what Achilli intends to do, it'd be great. Unfortunately, I don't trust the man anymore as a developer or writer. He too frequently ignores, contradicts, or changes established canon (instead of building on it) to create a too specific version of the setting, and then tell us this is the only way it is. I often find his ideas to be perfectly fine for an individual chronicle, but to have eliminated way too many options for other STs that were available in earlier editions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T14:31:01-07:00","id":1477023,"title":"","content":"The Umbra desperately needs a source book like Damnation City for the local Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T15:06:24-07:00","id":1477027,"title":"","content":"The umbra I've found largely prevents this from feeling like a werewolf game, and things being able to dedicate your clothes and very rarely frenzying unless your rage is absurdly high pretty much destroys it. When your zipping through dimensions like you've got a Rick Sanchez portal-gun, while clothed and clear thinking, and wielding a silver sword, any relation to werewolf is distant at best. You're pretty much a Druid/Barbarian multi-class in a Captain Planet style superhero story at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T16:31:31-07:00","id":1477031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477027#post1477027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The umbra I've found largely prevents this from feeling like a werewolf game, and things being able to dedicate your clothes and very rarely frenzying unless your rage is absurdly high pretty much destroys it. When your zipping through dimensions like you've got a Rick Sanchez portal-gun, while clothed and clear thinking, and wielding a silver sword, any relation to werewolf is distant at best. You're pretty much a Druid/Barbarian multi-class in a Captain Planet style superhero story at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, WtA is not really a game about typical werewolves. Even in 1st ed, it was clear the focus was less on the horror of being a werewolf and more on the horror that was fighting the Wyrm. Unless you are looking at medieval depictions of werewolves, WtA's pretty much as you said Druid/Barbarian defender of nature over a werewolf game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T16:39:14-07:00","id":1477033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477031#post1477031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, WtA is not really a game about typical werewolves. Even in 1st ed, it was clear the focus was less on the horror of being a werewolf and more on the horror that was fighting the Wyrm. Unless you are looking at medieval depictions of werewolves, WtA's pretty much as you said Druid/Barbarian defender of nature over a werewolf game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I think is what they\u2019re trying to change with 5th. I\u2019m I mean I agree with the rest of you, and Black Fox pretty much put words to my experience with the umbra a lot of the time. It may be why I prefer the hisil a lot of the time, which is largely a penumbra focus, really. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to run a personal horror werewolf game at some point. No tribes, just blind cubs. But maybe I should just leave that to forsaken which has the established mechanics and lore for it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T20:25:43-07:00","id":1477051,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, werewolves have maintained a lot more of their mythological/folklore variety in pop-culture compared to vampires. Whereas the Gothic horror authors coalesced relatively cohesively around a central idea of &quot;vampire&quot; that's remained fairly consistent over the past two centuries of pop-culture, werewolves never really got that treatment. While people can argue about preferences over &quot;only changes under the full moon, and has no choice,&quot; to, &quot;can change whenever they want,&quot; you don't really have any real coherent idea that some part of that spectrum excludes a story from being about werewolves. Likewise, while folklore doesn't really have anything like werewolves with five different forms, the five forms in WtA all reflect different folkore about what a human that's become a werewolf actually turns into.<br /> <br /> Do a quick Google of &quot;best werewolf movies,&quot; and you quickly find a lot more variety to werewolves, and the kind of stories werewolves are used in, than you get with a lot of the other Universal/Hammer horror monsters<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T02:20:33-07:00","id":1477064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477033#post1477033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I think is what they\u2019re trying to change with 5th.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this change is the whole problem.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: the Apocalypse isn't about personal horror and was never meant to be. It is about Rage, but more to the point, the <u><i>permission</i></u> to Rage. The core premise is to have a cathartic experience where, be it the Wyrm, Humanity, Spirits, or the many problems within the Garou society itself, you face the things that make you angry and you're allowed to embrace this anger instead of bottle it. Everything else builds up from this premise directly or tangentially.<br /> <br /> The horror in the game is mostly outside. It is in the Wyrm. It is in Garou that chose to let their purpose become a justification for evil. It is in the evils that corruption, ignorance or bad choices cause upon the world. There is a seed of personal horror in the fact that you may still fall to temptation and become part of the problem, but ultimately the power to not follow this path is almost entirely on your hands (staving off the worse of frenzy isn't really that hard and isn't meant to be).<br /> <br /> Other than that, it is Drama and Tragedy, not horror. The themes of soldiers doomed to live in war, ever barred from sharing the peace they fight for. A life guided by violence, from violence and to violence. The classic tragic cycle of fighting against prophecy while causing it through your mistakes to happen. Isolation from family and friends to go to a war you won't come back from. Those and so many others are <b>not</b> horror themes and never were. They're personal, for sure, but they're about honor, glory and wisdom, not mere survival.<br /> <br /> I have my reasons to not like Apocalypse a lot, but I can't say it isn't an awesome game when well run. But it isn't Forsaken, it isn't about a curse or about feeling cursed, except in the tragic takes of the idea of being cursed with awesomeness, powers and responsibility and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T03:02:42-07:00","id":1477068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477051#post1477051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, werewolves have maintained a lot more of their mythological/folklore variety in pop-culture compared to vampires. Whereas the Gothic horror authors coalesced relatively cohesively around a central idea of &quot;vampire&quot; that's remained fairly consistent over the past two centuries of pop-culture, werewolves never really got that treatment. While people can argue about preferences over &quot;only changes under the full moon, and has no choice,&quot; to, &quot;can change whenever they want,&quot; you don't really have any real coherent idea that some part of that spectrum excludes a story from being about werewolves. Likewise, while folklore doesn't really have anything like werewolves with five different forms, the five forms in WtA all reflect different folkore about what a human that's become a werewolf actually turns into.<br /> <br /> Do a quick Google of &quot;best werewolf movies,&quot; and you quickly find a lot more variety to werewolves, and the kind of stories werewolves are used in, than you get with a lot of the other Universal/Hammer horror monsters</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, digging into older werewolf lore shows some truly interesting figures, such as the bedandanti and the Finnish werewolf weddings.<br /> <br /> However, despite the flexibility of the werewolf, I think people seeking a werewolf game want a few specific things;<br /> <br /> 1. Loss of control<br /> 2. Monster inside scaring the person<br /> 3. Painful transformations<br /> 4. Full moon change without control<br /> 5. Violent slaughter without the human side's consent.<br /> <br /> And while WtA DOES offer these, it is not the whole game. Essentially, take Gaia, the Wyrm, the War of Apocalypse (, the breeds, the auspices) and such off and I think that is more what people seek. Essentially a game of dealing with a human and monster side.<br /> <br /> Which is very close to Vampire, which is why WtA went its own direction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T03:24:30-07:00","id":1477071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477064#post1477064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf: the Apocalypse isn't about personal horror and was never meant to be. It is about Rage, but more to the point, the <u><i>permission</i></u> to Rage. The core premise is to have a cathartic experience where, be it the Wyrm, Humanity, Spirits, or the many problems within the Garou society itself, you face the things that make you angry and you're allowed to embrace this anger instead of bottle it. Everything else builds up from this premise directly or tangentially.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> &quot;Personal Horror&quot; is the tag-line of VtM, not the WoD in general. The 1st edition of WtA uses the expression &quot;Savage Horror&quot; on page 59. By the 2nd Edition core book, the inner Titlepage (after the comic) reads: <b>A storytelling game of savage horror</b> by Mark Rein-Hagen with Robert Hatch and Bill Bridges<br /> <br /> Still even 2nd Edition only uses the term once more, on page 29: You are going to weave wondrous tales - stories of peril, fear, and <b>savage horror</b>.<br /> <br /> Personal Horror does not appear to be mentioned in WtA (although DriveThruRPG's PDF sometimes have misinterpreted characters and therefore text search is not optimal).<br /> <br /> Also, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> on the premise, that one letting go of the Rage is meant to be a cathartic experience for the garou. In our LARP we always double check our plots, so the follow the guideline &quot;Violence is always an option&quot;. It might not be the best option, the safest, but usually it is an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 03-23-2022, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T04:13:58-07:00","id":1477074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477068#post1477068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, despite the flexibility of the werewolf, I think people seeking a werewolf game want a few specific things;<br /> 1. Loss of control<br /> 2. Monster inside scaring the person<br /> 3. Painful transformations<br /> 4. Full moon change without control<br /> 5. Violent slaughter without the human side's consent.<br /> <br /> And while WtA DOES offer these, it is not the whole game. Essentially, take Gaia, the Wyrm, the War of Apocalypse (, the breeds, the auspices) and such off and I think that is more what people seek. Essentially a game of dealing with a human and monster side.<br /> <br /> Which is very close to Vampire, which is why WtA went its own direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I don't want these things in my games, and I don't think to many other people I know are seeking for it.<br /> <br /> As far as loss of control goes, sure, there are players who want that for their characters and as their experience in game. Me, personally, not so much. Still, it is worth mentioning, that there is a difference to loosing control to one's emotions, as opposed to an outside force. There is no submission there, when a garou looses control, the garou is dominating the surroundings, usually.<br /> <br /> There have been players who dwelled in what being a garou meant for their character. Usually players who started out as cubs. Most players don't explore that anymore, once they have some experience with the game. At least not in my experience.<br /> <br /> I never had, to my knowledge, contact with anyone, who wanted the physical change to be painful. Character groth and personality shifts due to emotionally painful events, sure, but that's something else.<br /> <br /> Also, I never experienced any player who wanted to be forced to shift on the full moon. Or loose control due to the moon. Even those players I know, who really want to loose control do want to loose it because of the emotional state of their character, as triggered by the situation they see themselves confronted by, but not by an external trigger...<br /> <br /> Slaughter without the human side's consent also is kind of close to loosing control. In any case, all the WtA I play have the garou as a single person. There is no Dr. Jeckel and Mr. Hyde where the monster has it's own personality and the garou in homid form thinks of the Crinos &quot;That's not me, that's the moster&quot;. I mean that could happen, I guess, especially if the Gnosis is so low, that one doesn't remember Frenzy, but even then, the other garou would tell the character, that is what you did, not what some monster did.<br /> <br /> What I want from WtA specifically, as a player, would be something like this:<br /> 1. Power - Just with any other game, I want to be a protagonist that has some ability to change things and possibly is special compared to the average character in the game world. I don't like, for example, a game like Paranoia, where the character is meant to be subject of the computer's rule.<br /> 2. Teamwork - Garou as a sept and within a pack usually work for the same goal. As compared to for example Vampire LARP, with a lot of backstabbing, intrigue and often out-of-game grievances stemming from these, the werewolf game is more friendly. Players are competing for sept offices, who's pack is getting the next mission and so on. There are hostilities, but they do not fill the game and you don't have to be paranoid to survive...<br /> 3. Being the Hero - Garou have a mission and while their means are questionable (by human standards and Ragabashs everywhere) they believe in their cause and see themselves as the heros and feel good about what they do. I want my character to have that satisfaction. I don't usually want plots where victories are only partial or where every win is countered by to losses right away. This can bring a sense of dread, but, like I said, I don't need that.<br /> <br /> So, these are rather general statements. I like WtA for it's Setting, or most of it. That being 2nd Edition and some aspects of revised. That's what we were playing, when I started the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T04:20:36-07:00","id":1477075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477071#post1477071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> on the premise, that one letting go of the Rage is meant to be a cathartic experience for the garou. In our LARP we always double check our plots, so the follow the guideline &quot;Violence is always an option&quot;. It might not be the best option, the safest, but usually it is an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>This and a huge part of the nature of the game is that the antagonists are things that frustrate and make people feel powerless IRL. Racism, capitalism, poverty, pollution, global warming, misogyny, etc. The Rage in-game is the cleansing fire that can burn them away but also can destroy something good as it spreads.<br /> <br /> Essentially, it is making pollution a physical target and punching it.<br /> <br /> This is why the Captain Planet insult always feels hollow to me. Because not only are these issues not just things in cartoons, but the nature of WtA goes very much into the punk side of Gothic Punk. It is saying fuck you to how things are and fighting for how things could be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T06:06:51-07:00","id":1477080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477068#post1477068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, despite the flexibility of the werewolf, I think people seeking a werewolf game want a few specific things;</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this list based on? I'm certain there are people that would consider the list &quot;essential&quot; but I know lots of people that would disagree with some or all of it as essential to a werewolf game (and there are enough games that let you play werewolves that don't abide by this list precisely that it seems like it fails to really capture a core idea of what a werewolf game needs to offer).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T07:58:28-07:00","id":1477089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477080#post1477080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is this list based on? I'm certain there are people that would consider the list &quot;essential&quot; but I know lots of people that would disagree with some or all of it as essential to a werewolf game (and there are enough games that let you play werewolves that don't abide by this list precisely that it seems like it fails to really capture a core idea of what a werewolf game needs to offer).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is based on things that I've seen people out of here focus on in werewolf media. It is by no means definitive, but things I've seen and heard make a werewolf story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T08:15:30-07:00","id":1477092,"title":"","content":"I don't consider myself a ''role play gamer''. I play only wod and cod, and mostly only werewolf.<br /> Honestly, I seek and want in WtA and from their protagonists many things that the modern players seems to avoid, but despite it, throwing away hope from Wta, making Gaia dead and make the war loss, is nonsense. The best thing about Werewolf the Apocalypse, to me, it's the little spark of hope that can become a fire, a fire that can redeem or burn the garou. The fact that even the god-like enemies and the untouchable CEO of Pentex can still feel a shake on their back when they hear the howls of Gaia's warriors, it's everything in my chronicles.<br /> I like the first edition vibe, where garou were monsters tout court, but heroes of their legacies, maybe heroes or maybe villains for humanity.<br /> The sort of raw, realistic street level brutality red in tooth and claw. I never had the captain planet problem. Tradition vs progress, bigotry, animal dominance and violence were all great ingredients for our games, keeping us focused on the tragedy without even thinking about the garou as good people for humanity, with the logical exceptions.<br /> I hope the game will have enough to make me de-olding my games in the right way for my party. That's all I have to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T13:20:29-07:00","id":1477115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477089#post1477089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is based on things that I've seen people out of here focus on in werewolf media. It is by no means definitive, but things I've seen and heard make a werewolf story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Upon reading your own response here, do you not feel that it comes off as a pretty weak defense of that list?<br /> <br /> It's anecdote. It doesn't even try to look at what werewolf fiction is out there and popular to help get around the anecdotal side of things. It doesn't try to argue about how those anecdotes are supposed to translate from stories to games (and that's pretty important, since playing a game about werewolves is a different consideration than consuming a story about them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T16:50:59-07:00","id":1477133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477115#post1477115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Upon reading your own response here, do you not feel that it comes off as a pretty weak defense of that list?<br /> <br /> It's anecdote. It doesn't even try to look at what werewolf fiction is out there and popular to help get around the anecdotal side of things. It doesn't try to argue about how those anecdotes are supposed to translate from stories to games (and that's pretty important, since playing a game about werewolves is a different consideration than consuming a story about them).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, those are things I've seen people want of their werewolf media. It was not written with any sort of gameplay in mind, as it's simply a list of what I've seen people use as markers of a 'good' werewolf media. It is anecdotal, but I feel they do showcase what is the core of the issue; The 'classic' werewolf is a person cursed to be one in some way and struggling with it.<br /> <br /> Does this fit with folklore? Nope. Are all werewolf movies like that? No, but the ones I've seen people tote as the definition are (An American Werewolf in London, The Howling and Van Helsing.)<br /> <br /> Does it make for a good game? Not really, at best it'd be just a weaker copy of Vampire. But I don't think that is the main consideration when I see people calling WtA out on not being about werewolves.<br /> <br /> I think this is why the Bite in BNS was introduced. It fits better with the fantasy of being turned into a cursed monster than the whole born into it aspect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T17:08:30-07:00","id":1477136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477075#post1477075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, it is making pollution a physical target and punching it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477075#post1477075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why the Captain Planet insult always feels hollow to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is hollow. It is the ill thought &quot;insult&quot; of someone that dislikes the game just out of prejudice, like the many that think Garou are just frenzied melee machines only because this is their starting advantage.<br /> <br /> One thing I must say, as a Vampire fan first and foremost: <b><u>there's nothing fucking wrong with being Captain Planet</u></b>. It is like offending VtM because it is just a Karloff's Dracula rip-off. Ahn, it isn't, and sometimes it is and still isn't a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T08:37:48-07:00","id":1477216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477136#post1477136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is hollow. It is the ill thought &quot;insult&quot; of someone that dislikes the game just out of prejudice, like the many that think Garou are just frenzied melee machines only because this is their starting advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>And because WoD's primary and most popular game VtM describes them as such.<br /> <br /> I mean, garou should (frenzy or not) make use of their melee prowess and rip vampires apart. Those vampires that flee and survive should tell exactly that to other vampires and subsequently it is the way the in-universe section of Clanbooks and such describe the werewolves.<br /> <br /> It isn't the job of VtM books to set the record straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T13:40:15-07:00","id":1477264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477068#post1477068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, despite the flexibility of the werewolf, I think people seeking a werewolf game want a few specific things;<br /> <br /> 1. Loss of control<br /> 2. Monster inside scaring the person<br /> 3. Painful transformations<br /> 4. Full moon change without control<br /> 5. Violent slaughter without the human side's consent.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if that is what most players actually want. All of those things take away from player agency. Instead of letting players decide what their characters do, these points would hijack that. And players hate that. It's not fun for them. Even in Vampire which states it is a game of personal horror and wants PCs to explore the consequences of doing evil, 1) the rules that take away agency are used only some of the time, and 2) most players I see downplay the personal horror aspect and want to live out power fulfillment fantasies.<br /> <br /> What I do think some players want is to see more of the classic werewolf <i>tropes</i> in the setting. (And the tropes can be varied, actual folklore, movies, and stories about werewolves often do not agree - and that's fine.) Too often, the game ignores them. As you say, the setting actually <u>does</u> have concepts that can fulfill those tropes. They just aren't utilized. And we almost never saw them in setting sourcebooks, so it's easy for players to overlook.<br /> <br /> But WtA does have concepts like Lunatics that meet almost everything you laid out above. But Lunatics as a concept is rarely mentioned again outside a rare 1e supplement. But what would have happened, if we saw at least one Lunatic NPC in each of the Rage books, exploring different ways that individual Lunatic impacts the local setting, and how PCs might interact with that person?<br /> <br /> We have the concept of Ronins, which would be a great place to explore a Garou who could have a life totally different from the culture of the Garou Nation. Ronin could easily be used to explore alternate takes on the werewolf (conforming more to people's expectations) while not invalidating anything about the setting. And we could have been given more tools a how to incorporate a Ronin PC with a traditional Garou pack, making Ronin + Garou PC party just as easy as a Vampire including a Caitiff with Clans. But the game didn't so many STs wouldn't know how to run a game with this odd PC, so they discourage players from even making such a character. (I remember we have talked extensively about how Ronin can play a greater role in the game on the past ion several different threads.)<br /> <br /> There's actually a lot of Merits and Flaws that mirror these tropes too. You can create Garou who are banned or forced to change depending on the cycle of the moon or other things, that have the folklore attributes of middle digits being equal length, hairy palms, or eyebrows that meet together, or even have the Larry Talbot pentagram on their hand, or vulnerabilty to wolfsbane. It's just that we don't see these Flaws for actual NPCs. But what would happen, if there was a noticeable number of NPCs that had these? Or we might see a specific family of Garou consistently show these traits giving a reason why this element showed up in human cultural lore about werewolves.<br /> <br /> In general, if the Rage books had a section for non-tribal Garou, and included a few NPCs that matched some of the genre/trope expectations of pop culture, I think it would have strengthened the game. And people would be more likely to see the game as being part of the mainstream werewolf genre instead of something apart from it.<br /> <br /> This is what I try to do in my chronicles, and I have had success with it. My players seem to like it. It doesn't fundamentally change the setting, but it reminds the players that this is a game about werewolves, and not some fantasy species.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T14:12:01-07:00","id":1477268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477264#post1477264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, if the Rage books had a section for non-tribal Garou, and included a few NPCs that matched some of the genre/trope expectations of pop culture, I think it would have strengthened the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. I think, it would have been a different game. Could be better or worse.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't even start with the assumption that there is a significant number of potential players who feel that WtA as is doesn't satisfy their needs for Werewolf pop-culture tropes in their RPG hobby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T14:22:08-07:00","id":1477271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477264#post1477264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I do think some players want is to see more of the classic werewolf <i>tropes</i> in the setting. (And the tropes can be varied, actual folklore, movies, and stories about werewolves often do not agree - and that's fine.) Too often, the game ignores them. As you say, the setting actually <u>does</u> have concepts that can fulfill those tropes. They just aren't utilized. And we almost never saw them in setting sourcebooks, so it's easy for players to overlook.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you hit the nail on the head. The tropes are what people seek.<br /> <br /> I think the sidelining of the ronin came about due to WtA being so focused on the Gaians vs Wyrm thing, that those who might not fit in just did not have room in the setting. After all, within those 12 tribes there already were numerous ways to fight the Wyrm and that ronin basically are removed from the core gameplay loop entirely. Having a ronin PC among tribe PCs would have made one player much more limited than the others. A kindred can be unaligned and still have the same access to powers as those in a sect, while a ronin is basically shit out of luck in every aspect.<br /> <br /> It is no wonder that Ghost Wolves are such an integral part of Forsaken, as the free agents and those unaligned from the tribes.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T14:29:04-07:00","id":1477272,"title":"","content":"The problem is that a bunch of NPCs in supplements only really impact people that are already fans of the game to be buying and reading deeply into a bunch of supplements. If you don't like the lack of certain pop-culture tropes getting focus in the core book, why are you going to keep buying and reading to find them in supplements? If you like WtA as it's presented in the core books, why would you want the supplements to constantly harp on this other stuff?<br /> <br /> Forsaken 2e implements a lot of these tropes in the Harmony system (basically they tend to be the result of being out of balance and at the extremes of Harmony)... and then doesn't really bother talking about it much. It's obvious from the core book without supplements bringing up examples a lot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T15:32:46-07:00","id":1477277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477271#post1477271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tropes are what people seek.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I do not.<br /> <br /> Which specific tropes are you even talking about?<br /> I mean, tv tropes has several pages on werewolf related tropes, but nothing that isn't somehow represented in the game. Also, werewolves seem to mainly derive their mythology from early eras of TV and film. I can't recall a werewolf tale in Grimm's Fairytales or any other older German legend. Werebeasts, sure, are found in the myths of mankind but werewolves specifically.<br /> <br /> If I wanted a &quot;League of Extraordinary Gentleman&quot;-like Setting, with unaffiliated werewolves and clan-less vampires and non-horus affiliated Mummies and what not, I'd probably not choose to play WoD, but maybe <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Everlasting_(role-playing_game)\" target=\"_blank\">Everlasting</a>. Or one of the many other games with supernatural folks. Hell, even Buffy/Angle-RPG or Monte Cook's WoD.<br /> <br /> But that is not what I seek. I don't just want a game world in which the tropes are working.<br /> I want the shamanism, the fight for a good cause, the tribal brotherhood, the hypocrisy, and all that.<br /> I find the need for the tropes to be fulfilled are an obstruction to the game.<ul><li>Unsoakable Silver Damage is a menace, mechanically, more difficult to soak I get, but no dice at all - design flaw.</li> <li>Transformation and Frenzy at the full moon - the difficulties for Rage rolls at the full moon are way to low. Moots are supposed to happen, but seriously, you can't have a session with more than just fluff set at the full moon without some entering a frenzy - The Rite of the Lodge (not sure about the name) is protecting the get of fenris, all other tribes should have killed each other off for insisting to meet at full moons.</li> <li>Wolvesbane and mistletow - I'm those aren't a thing in WtA.</li> <li>Religious symbols - well True Faith has it's own rules and there is a rarely a description on its effects on garou, but iirc Inquisition sourcebook did provide rules. I'm quite indifferent if this should have a larger part in WtA.</li> <li>Not remembering what happened during transformation - That would be a ill-conceived if the player would play the character and then do as if the character wouldn't remember. But WtA has memory loss as a possibility during Frenzy and that is okay.</li> <li>Werewolves playing basket ball - is that a real thing or just Michael J. Fox's idea of a werewolf.</li> <li>Werewolves hate vampires - according to tvtropes website this trope is originating from the WoD games. Funny. I like that trope in my WtA game.</li> <li>Change only at full moon - I wouldn't want a where the character could just what makes them special only once every 28 days. Would you play a D&amp;D wizard, if spellcasting was limited to specific dates? I never had a player ask for something like that and I can't imagine it will ever happen.</li> <li>Reverting back to human form on death - check. WtA has it, no player ever asked to have that ability for the character, though.</li> <li>Social outcast - WtA has the Curse, so that trope also is in the game.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> So, which tropes are needed to be represented more in the game?<br /> What do player ask for, really?<br /> <br /> Like I said, I never had players who had a specific idea of a werewolf form legend, folklore or any other source and wanted that characteristics reproduced in the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T19:16:47-07:00","id":1477296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477277#post1477277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I do not.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Neither do I. Anecdotal as it might be, I am only repeating what I've heard from other people.<br /> <br /> Also, I think it should be noted most people who think like this probably won't end up playing WtA, coming to the forums, joining a LARP or taking part in discussions like this. They see a werewolf game, check it out, find it is not to their liking and move on.<br /> <br /> If you expect to be playing a cursed being trying to deal with being a werewolf and instead get a shamanistic tale of Nature versus Technology, it can put you off.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T20:42:48-07:00","id":1477303,"title":"","content":"It's also been a good 30 years since anyone picked up WtA purely blind to what's actually inside of it. Sure, it might still happens, but I find it extremely unlikely that it happens in any meaningful fashion these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T03:16:13-07:00","id":1477321,"title":"","content":"With the loss of next door hobby and comic book stores, you might be right.<br /> <br /> Unless one picks it up from one's parents', older sibling's or cousin's bookshelf....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T04:42:21-07:00","id":1477325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476534-why-the-struggle-matters?p=1477321#post1477321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the loss of next door hobby and comic book stores, you might be right.<br /> <br /> Unless one picks it up from one's parents', older sibling's or cousin's bookshelf....</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they hear about the game online and check it out on Drivethru?<br /> <br /> Seriously, a lot of RPing is happening online and PDFs are often prefered over physical books. Even if it was yeeeears ago, I got into WtA through the White Wolf site for the game.<br /> <br /> As well, when I was storytelling for a server, we had plenty of new people join in.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T09:26:16-07:00","id":1477446,"title":"","content":"Yeah, while I don't think the loss of brick-and-mortar hobby stores is a good thing, I hardly think we had more new players back then to any game whatsoever. Those shops are nice and good, but ultimately very niche and hard for the &quot;non-initiated&quot; to find and the owners to keep. The hobby is far more accessible and known through the online world, and more people come to it than ever. Those people also get a lot more info before buying.<br /> <br /> Today the almost blind purchase solely based on randomly finding the cover then perusing the book is by far the exception, not the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}